 "acceptance": "PASS iff all of: solver rc 20; solver status lines (log with only '\\r' removed, lines starting with 's') exactly ['s UNSATISFIABLE']; checker rc 0; checker log with only '\\r' removed has a line exactly 's VERIFIED' and contains neither 's NOT VERIFIED' nor 's TIMEOUT'; no safety stop; solver and checker writer threads ok with no close error and finished, written == formula length, and sha256 of the bytes each actually wrote == the bound hash (formula: BINDING/worker r2 strengthened hash; leaf: parent binding RESULT leaf hash == MANIFEST cnf_sha256); the parent relay saw the FIFO EOF, read R > 0 proof bytes and delivered D bytes to the checker with R == D, equal sha256 of the bytes read and the bytes delivered, no delivery, drain or close error, nothing withheld, and its thread finished; the checker's own 'c finished parsing, read N bytes from proof file' line is present with N == D (absent line: fail-closed; drat-trim.c L986-988, L1107-1115: N == D means the delivered stream was consumed to EOF and well-formed); stricter than the brief: drat-trim's 'c parsing input formula' line reports the header's variable and clause counts and the checker log has no 'early EOF' or 'clauses less than expected' warning; no driver SIGTERM latched during the pipeline or at evaluation, no lane-scanner failure latched, the scanner thread stopped, every started worker thread finished, no helper survivor. The proof-stream sha256 and byte count (relay read side) are recorded as provenance; they do not make a proof correct, only drat-trim's verdict on the delivered bytes does. Anything else is UNKNOWN, with reasons (SAT report, proof rejection, feed mismatch, timeout, guard stop, writer error, other). After a SAT report (rc 10 or 's SATISFIABLE') the model stays in the solver log and the desk launches nothing more; after a floor or safety stop (including a spawn error, a latched SIGTERM, a scanner failure, an unfinished thread, a live scanner or a helper survivor) the desk launches nothing more; any other UNKNOWN continues with the next item. No retries without parent approval.",
 "gate": "Before each launch a fresh lane scan (native solver/checker processes plus python processes whose cwd or argv lies in the lane or a review/moqls8-* desk, excluding this desk's driver and children; python counts as busy if its CPU use over a 2 s libproc window is >= 50%; lane RSS conservatively includes every such python, busy or not) and a fresh statvfs: launch only if lane busy + 4 <= 4 (v6c: this desk counts cadical, drat-trim, its own driver and one transient helper), lane RSS (all other lane processes, a worker GB pipeline included) + max(fresh measured desk RSS, projected; an unreadable desk RSS refuses) <= 11 GiB (v6: parent phys-1 pipeline resource amendment dc1eaed0...b2a8: one scientific pipeline) and free >= 12,200,000,000 + 80 MiB. Stricter than the brief: two consecutive passing checks 60 s apart are required, so a launch never rides a transient gap of the priority worker pipeline. Otherwise sleep 60 s and re-check; total gate wait per run bounded by 600 s (v6c), then stop and report deferral. No launch at or after 2026-10-22 18:59:33 PDT (host clock; chunk fit: spawn + backstop + 120 s reap + 60 s margin <= owned_compute_settled_by - 180 s), and (v6c) no native spawn unless driver elapsed + the item's backstop <= 10620 s. Formula launches additionally need the parent observer v3 (control/resource-observer-live-v3.jsonl, 10 s cadence; rule: stability addendum v1 9aff1085..., path: addendum v2 6ddac862...) to show, from complete JSON lines with tz-aware strictly increasing timestamps: last sample 0 <= age <= 30 s with free >= 13,500,000,000 + 80 MiB, >= 25 samples spanning >= 290 s within the last 300 s, and a max peak-to-later free drop over that window <= max(300,000,000, (free_last - 13,500,000,000) / 12); a malformed complete line, an absent, unreadable or stale monitor refuses the launch (fail closed); the rule and a fresh statvfs are re-read at the launch decision. Controls keep the plain fresh gate. Any recorded helper survivor refuses every launch. Projected peak = formulas: max(1.5 x worker aggregate peak of the formula's source template leaf (the worker's 900 s attempt; no worker run of a strengthened formula exists), 9 GiB) (v6); leaves are refused by v6; self-tests 512 MiB.",
 "in_flight_stops": "In flight, every 0.25 s: desk aggregate RSS (driver + live children, libproc; a live child unreadable twice in a row is a guard failure) and free space; a scanner thread publishes lane scans every >= 1 s (helpers under 8 s deadlines; any failed reading is latched). SIGTERM own children if a lane reading failed, a failure is latched or the reading is older than 30 s, lane RSS (other lane processes, GB included, + max(desk measured, desk reservation = projected)) > 11 GiB, desk aggregate > projected + 0.5 GiB, free < 12,000,000,000, a child-output sink overflow (> 32 MiB per log) or sink failure (v6c), other lane busy + 4 > 4 (v6c), driver elapsed > 10620 s (v6c chunk deadline), wall > 10260 s from the native spawn (600 s for controls; cadical -t 6300, drat-trim -t 10020), the host clock reaches 2026-10-22 21:50:00 PDT, the checker exits while the solver still runs, a solver spawn error, a helper survivor, any exception after the first fd, or the driver receives SIGTERM (also checked immediately before each spawn, before gate success and before the completion break, where a latched SIGTERM or scanner failure becomes the stop reason); then wait at most 120 s, never escalate; result UNKNOWN and the desk launches nothing more.",
